I've created a complete Notion-like workspace application for you! Here's what was built:

## 📦 What You Got

**Backend**: Python + Flask with SQLite database  
**Frontend**: Vanilla JavaScript with accessible controls  
**Storage**: SQLite (persists data across restarts)

## 🚀 Quick Start

```sh
cd /workspace
PORT=8765 sh start.sh
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8765/ in your browser.

## ✨ Features Implemented

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Create pages** | Click `+` in the sidebar |
| **Add blocks** | Unlimited text blocks per page |
| **Edit blocks** | Click any block to edit content |
| **Delete blocks** | Hover over a block, click × button |
| **Delete pages** | Hover over page item, click × button |
| **Keyboard access** | Tab navigation between all controls |
| **Persistent storage** | SQLite database at `app/blocks.db` |

## 📁 Files Created

```
/workspace/
├── start.sh                 # Start script (runs uv sync + app)
├── README.md                # Documentation
└── app/
    ├── app.py               # Flask API backend
    ├── database.py          # SQLite module
    ├── templates/index.html # HTML template
    └── static/
        ├── css/style.css    # Styling
        └── js/app.js        # Frontend logic
```

## 🎯 Usage

**Start**: `PORT=8765 sh start.sh`  
**Browse**: http://127.0.0.1:8765/

- Click `+` in sidebar to create pages
- Click any block to edit it
- Hover blocks/pages to see delete buttons
- Use Tab key for keyboard navigation

All data persists in SQLite database across restarts! 🎉
